Public archive of the International Institute of Tetric Physics (IITP) — a bilingual research site on the filotermetetrico: a thread of tetric monomers that can assume any form and function.

The polymer is composed of tetrions and tetric gluons. Its spectro-tetric wave is treated as the vacuum’s fundamental oscillation, organised through the primordial tetric nebula. Experimental work is presented as the campaign at the Large Tetrum Collider (LTC).

Default language is English. A header control switches the full archive to Italian.

